  "id": "unconscious-perception",
  "term": "unconscious perception",
  "definition": "Unconscious perception is the idea that a stimulus can influence a person’s response even when they do not report being aware of it. In this context, evidence for it comes from tasks where a masked prime affects performance, though such effects may sometimes reflect very weak conscious experience rather than a complete lack of awareness.",
